Here are 5 specific, actionable recommendations for the Include Client error tracking gate:

1. Implement client error tracking in the `ErrorController` class located at `com.example.project.web.controller.ErrorController.java`. Create a new method `handleClientError()` that logs errors with the `@Loggable` annotation and returns an HTTP response with a 500 status code. This will ensure that client-side errors are properly tracked and logged.

Example implementation:
```java
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.ControllerAdvice;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.ExceptionHandler;

@ControllerAdvice
public class ErrorController {
    @ExceptionHandler(value = Exception.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleClientError(Exception e) {
        // Log error with @Loggable annotation
        @Loggable
        logger.error("Client error occurred", e);

        // Return HTTP response with 500 status code
        return new ResponseEntity<>(new ErrorResponse("Internal Server Error"), HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```
2. Add a client error tracking implementation to the `UserController` class located at `com.example.project.web.controller.UserController.java`. Create a new method `getUser()` that logs errors with the `@Loggable` annotation and returns an HTTP response with a 500 status code if the user is not found.

Example implementation:
