4. Consider implementing a more sophisticated rate limiter that takes into account factors such as request latency and IP address. For example, you can use the `Redis` cache to store rate limit information for each IP address.

```java
@Configuration
public class RedisThrottlingConfig {

    @Bean
    public RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate() {
        return new RedisTemplate<>();
    }

    @Bean
    public ThrottlingFilter throttlingFilter(RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate) {
        return new RedisThrottlingFilter(redisTemplate);
    }
}

public class RedisThrottlingFilter extends AbstractRequestFilter {

    private final RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate;

    public RedisThrottlingFilter(RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate) {
        this.redisTemplate = redisTemplate;
    }

    @Override
